SCST +caw-abort-reclaim.7: the new session of an I_T nexus takes the PR registrant from any
earlier session of that nexus, not only from one already shutting down.

.6 (lab/scst-pr-registrant-handoff.patch) moved the registrant to a new session's tgt_dev only
when the tgt_dev holding it belonged to a session no longer SCST_SESS_SPH_READY. On a path flap
that never held. Measured on the MXFS lab target, 2026-10-24 00:52:29Z (2/net/mesh/mpath
path_flap, test18, pool-02): the cut path's old connection is closed only as the initiator logs
in again ("Connection ... unexpectedly closed", NEXUS_LOSS_SESS), the new session is created at
once with the same ISID, and iscsi-scst calls scst_unregister_session() for the old session only
when it frees it ("Freeing session ...", 00:52:30Z). So the new tgt_dev met the registrant on a
session still READY, left it there, and the new session's first 16 writes were refused
RESERVATION CONFLICT ("PR: moving reg" was never logged for test18; the PREEMPT AND ABORT that
followed reported the earlier session at shut_phase 0).

A registration belongs to the I_T nexus and survives its loss; a new session of the nexus (an
iSCSI login with an existing ISID is a reinstatement) replaces the old one. The new tgt_dev now
takes the registrant from any other session of the nexus, whatever its shut_phase, and the log
line names that phase. The earlier session's commands still in flight stay inside PREEMPT AND
ABORT's reach through .6's scst_pr_abort_nexus_sessions().

Applied to ~/src/scst on top of .6 and installed with scripts/scst_reload.sh (every rig VM
powered off first). Qualification: tests/scst_pr_bounds_check.sh, and
tests/scst_pr_abort_shutdown_race.sh's window, stress and handoff arms and its flap arm (the
path's cable cut for 4 s with scripts/san_net.sh while a direct writer runs on it, as a path row
cuts it), which fails on .6.

--- a/scst/include/scst_const.h
+++ b/scst/include/scst_const.h
@@ -114,8 +114,20 @@
  *      READY, and scst_pr_abort_reg() also aborts every other live
  *      session of the registrant's nexus on the device, so commands the
  *      old session admitted stay inside PREEMPT AND ABORT's reach.
+ *  .7  .6's handoff never fired on a path flap (measured 2026-10-24, MXFS
+ *      lab, 2/net/mesh/mpath path_flap): the cut path's old connection is
+ *      closed only as the initiator logs in again, iscsi-scst unregisters
+ *      the old session only when it frees it, so the new tgt_dev met the
+ *      registrant on a session still SCST_SESS_SPH_READY and left it there,
+ *      and the new session's first 16 writes were refused RESERVATION
+ *      CONFLICT.  The new tgt_dev of a nexus now takes the registrant from
+ *      any earlier session of the same nexus, whatever its shut_phase: a
+ *      new session of an I_T nexus replaces the old one (an iSCSI login
+ *      with an existing ISID is a reinstatement), and the earlier
+ *      session's commands stay inside PREEMPT AND ABORT's reach through
+ *      scst_pr_abort_nexus_sessions().
  */
-#define SCST_VERSION_STRING_SUFFIX	"+caw-abort-reclaim.6"
+#define SCST_VERSION_STRING_SUFFIX	"+caw-abort-reclaim.7"
 #define SCST_VERSION_STRING		SCST_VERSION_NAME SCST_VERSION_STRING_SUFFIX
 
 #ifdef SCST_BUILD_DATE
